firebase is Google's mobile and web app  development platform and it offers many  useful cloud services so you might  wonder what is the relationship between  firebase and Google cloud platform stick  around and I'll help you understand you  may know a firebase for all the features  it offers to enhance your client app  such as authentication analytics crash  reporting a be testing or in-app  messaging but firebase also has several  options to manage data and business  logic in the cloud to help you build  better apps this includes NoSQL database  service functions on device and  server-side machine learning api's blob  storage and more firebase is a wonderful  way for Android and web developers to  leverage Google cloud services without  exposing them to all the knobs and dials  of GCB in fact when you create a  firebase project it is a GCP project in  every aspect resource grouping identity  management and billing are all the same  this gives you a great way to start  using some cloud services before you  graduate into using GCP only when you  need to this is also important to any  user interested in building and mobile  or web app on top of an existing GCP  infrastructure while the look and feel  of the firebase console and cloud  console are clearly different you can  open the same project with either one if  you'd like to open an existing GCP  project in the firebase console to add  firebase specific functionality simply  select add a project and click through  the few setup steps once done all the  firebase KPIs will be automatically  enabled in your project if you have an  existing firebase project simply head  over to cloud console and open it there  with its identifier you should see and  be able to manipulate all of the project  resources finally you want to be careful  about deleting projects as deleting a  firebase project deletes the Google  cloud projects as well and all its  contained resources so now that you know  that a firebase project is also GCP  project let's focus on the three main  products that firebase and GCB have in  common  cloud storage a massively scalable blob  storage system  cloth functions a service compute  infrastructure for event-driven  programming and cloud 5 store a  massively scalable no SQL database these  three GCP products can be used in  firebase with additional mobile SDKs as  well as from the firebase CLI or command  line interface we'll cover the first one  now and the other two in the next video  so make sure you subscribe to this  channel cloud storage is a powerful yet  simple to use blob storage system and if  you have not heard of it then you should  check out the short data and storage  overview video link below cloud console  exposes the full power of cloud storage  while the firebase console exposes those  features that are most likely to be  relevant to firebase developers a  typical use case for firebase developers  using cloud storage is when managing  user generated content this is where the  firebase android/ios web  unity and C++ SDKs make it easy and yet  secure to upload and download objects  such as images straight from the app  similarly to GCB projects using App  Engine any new firebase project comes  with a default cloud storage bucket in  most cases firebase developers also use  this default storage location and thus  do not need to reference it by name  because of all the GCP and firebase  commonalities discussed so far any data  stored in cloud storage using firebase  can be further access and processed in  GCB and vice-versa  imagine for instance a firebase powered  mobile applications uploading pictures  to cloud storage it would be quite easy  for a cloud scheduler initiate a task to  resize crop delete or otherwise  manipulate all pictures in this default  bucket you can also feed these files  into other GCP big data products such as  bigquery data flow or even into our  machine learning products one thing that  you will want to note is how bucket  access control is different and  orthogonal cloud iam is used to control  access to buckets and objects from GCP  services on the other hand firebase  security rules control access only from  mobile application  that use the firebase SDKs so they're  you now know how data stored in cloud  storage can be equally accessed via  firebase powered app as well as from  your GCP hosted applications in the next  episode we'll discuss the two remaining  products common to both platforms cloud  functions and cloud fire store same  project and billing infrastructure  common cloud storage the two platforms  have a lot in common  and we're conceived to nicely complement  one another it's time to get going with  firebase or GCP or both thanks for  watching this video please like  subscribe comment share and look forward  to more GCP essentials videos  [Music]
 

